Hi,
I have a Panasonic Let's Note CF-SV1RDAKS (Tiger Lake, BIOS V2.00L22) and
eco_mode doesn't work. Reading the sysfs file gives an I/O error and
writing gives "Invalid argument".
After digging through the DSDT I found three issues specific to this newer
model:

\_SB.ECWR doesn't exist, the eco_mode_store function calls it and fails. On
CF-SV1 the correct call is SSET(0x80, value) not ECWR.
The SSET index for eco mode changed from 0x0A to 0x80 on this model.
The feature is gated behind _OSI("Windows 2006") via a method called
BLAI(). Without acpi_osi=! "acpi_osi=Windows 2006" "acpi_osi=Windows 2009"
as kernel parameters, the BIOS locks out the charge limit functionality
entirely.

With those kernel parameters and patching the driver to use
acpi_pcc_write_sset(pcc, 0x80, state) instead of the ECWR call, the sysfs
interface works. However eco mode persistence across reboots remains
unsolved. The EC appears to only accept charge limit commands during early
boot. This seems to match the known issue mentioned in
https://github.com/chantk/panasonic-laptop.

I have attached my dsdt.dsl if it helps.
Thanks

